# Temple of the Obsidian Moon — app

One PWA containing all seven halls. No build step, no backend.

    index.html          home screen / navigation
    pages/              the seven sections
    icons/  images/     app icons and artwork
    manifest.json  sw.js
    .well-known/assetlinks.json   <- SHA-256 still to fill in
    .nojekyll           keeps GitHub Pages from eating .well-known

## Deploy

Push to the repo root, Pages on, custom domain, Enforce HTTPS.
Then confirm `https://your-domain/.well-known/assetlinks.json` returns
JSON with an HTTP 200.

## Fill in assetlinks.json

Package name is already set to `com.obsidianmoontemple.temple`.
Replace `REPLACE_WITH_SHA256_FROM_PLAY_CONSOLE` with the SHA-256 of the
**app signing certificate** (Play Console -> Test and release -> Setup ->
App signing). Not the upload certificate.

## Build

    npm install -g @bubblewrap/cli
    bubblewrap init --manifest https://your-domain/manifest.json
    bubblewrap build

Target API 36. Output .aab, not .apk. Back up the keystore and its
passwords — losing them means never shipping an update to this listing.

## Changing anything later

Edit the file, bump `CACHE` in sw.js (`temple-v1` -> `temple-v2`), push.
Content updates need no new Play release; the app loads from the live site.
Only manifest, icon or package changes require a new .aab.

## Known / deliberate

- Portal, Altar and Kid Zone post to Google Apps Script endpoints. They're
  the only network dependencies; an offline bar appears when there's no
  connection rather than failing silently.
- The Obsidian Mirror's dialog sits slightly left of centre because the
  reset button is a flex sibling. Pre-existing, unchanged.
- No donation button — see notes before adding one to a paid app.
- Pantheon Gate is a separate release and is not included.
